enough **from that individual casino** to reach the next printed value. Stop before a break you cannot cross and lose unusable excess points; do not save them for later.\n\nFor example, from **8**: an award of **1** leaves you on 8; **2 or 3** takes you to **10**; **4 or 5** takes you to **12**.\n\nWhen several casinos pay you points on one turn, score them **individually, from smallest to largest**, choosing the order of equal-size casinos. You cannot combine their awards to cross a break. Several separate one-tile casinos therefore still cannot move a chip from 8 to 10.",
    "U025": "End and winner",
    "U026": "### End and winner\n\nAs soon as anyone draws **End of Game**, the game ends immediately. Do not take Play actions or initiate trades after that draw. Make the **final payout for all owned lots and all casinos touching The Strip**, using normal money, boss-point and scoring-break rules. Highest score after that payout wins. If tied for most points, the tied player with **most money** wins. The source gives no further tiebreak if both remain equal.\n\nIn this base game, a player also **wins immediately at 90+ points**.",
    "U027": "Two players",
    "U028": "### Two players\n\n**Do not build on F block.** During setup, **discard any F-lot card and draw a replacement**; use the two accepted A–E cards for starting lots and money. Discarded F cards remain discarded.\n\nDuring a turn, an **F-lot card places no marker**, but still causes the normal **owned-lot money and indicated casino money/points**. Discard it in its appropriate pile, then **repeat Draw** until an A, B, C, D or E card has been drawn and resolved. Only then proceed to Play. Thus multiple payouts can happen on one turn; you do not take actions between these draws. **End of Game still ends the game immediately** if drawn during this sequence."
